From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 12:35:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] server: add ios_thread_wait_links() for wait-chain inspection

struct thread_wait is private to thread.c, so the iOS [srv-stuck] probe
in queue_ios.c cannot walk a thread's active wait to check whether it
actually references a given object. This accessor answers that: 1 linked,
0 not linked, -1 no wait at all.

Compares against the WRAPPER object because that is what wait_on() stores
in entry->obj; object_sync_add_queue() resolves the sync object
internally.

